# One lint, and the half worth pinning is what it offers instead: `len` and `for x in <the builder>`
# are the two that need no per-type name at all, which is why `len` now comes first -- it is the
# same question `len` answered and the answer every other collection already gave.
lint 11:9 read it in place with len, b[i] or 'for x in <the builder>'
